<title>DUBAI: Oman oil refinery output dips January-July.</title>
<headline>Oman oil refinery output dips January-July.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Output from Oman's single oil refinery at Mina al Fahal averaged 70,225 barrels per day (bpd) between January and July this year, figures used in a monthly statistical bulletin compiled by the country's Ministry of Development shows.</p>
<p>Output the same period last year averaged 75,609 bpd.</p>
<p>The main products were long residue (37,940 bpd), gasoline (13,159 bpd), gas oil (14,605 bpd), jet A-1 (3,318 bpd) and butane (1,200 bpd).</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255</p>
